    {
      "title": "Exercise 2: Automatic Short Rows",
      "slug": "exercise-2-automatic-short-rows",
      "displayOrder": 3,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 832,
        "lessonOrder": 3
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<Style>\r\n.lightlist ul { padding-left:20px; list-style:none; }\r\n.lightlist li { margin-bottom:10px; }\r\n.lightlist li:before {'FontAwesome';\r\ncontent: '\\f00c';\r\nmargin:0 5px 0 -15px;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>NOTE:</b>\r\nThe goal of the AUTOMATIC wrap:<br>\r\n<ul class=\"lightlist\" style=\"list-style:none;\">\r\n<li>Put the instructed number of needles <b>LESS 1 needle</b> in hold OPPOSITE the carriage</li>\r\n<li>Knit across</li>\r\n<li><b>Pull one more needle into hold</b></li>\r\n<li>Knit back</li>\r\n<li>Repeat this as instructed</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/123/automatic-wrap1.jpg\">\r\n\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n<em>Your pattern instructions may tell you to hold 5 (8) needles, but for automatic wrap, you will initially hold 1 less stitch 4 (8).  Knit across, then pull one more stitch into hold and knit back (creating an automatic wrap)<br></em><br><b>By starting with the carriage on the right and holding the needles on the opposite side from the previous sample, this sample will be slanting in the opposite direction.</b><Br>\r\n        <ol>\r\n            <li>Cast on 20 (40) stitches</li>\r\n            <li>End with the carriage on the RIGHT</li>\r\n            <li>Set carriage to hold</li>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n            <li><i class=\"fa-solid fa-asterisk\"></i> Opposite the carriage, put 4 (7) needles in holding position</li>\r\n            <li>Knit RIGHT to LEFT</li>\r\n            <li>Pull one more needle to hold (this needle will wrap automatically)</li>\r\n            <li>Knit LEFT to RIGHT <i class=\"fa-solid fa-asterisk\"></i></li>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n            <li>Repeat from <i class=\"fa-solid fa-asterisk\"></i> to <i class=\"fa-solid fa-asterisk\"></i> until all needles are in hold</li>\r\n            <li>Tip: Cancel hold and knit1 row across all needles *</li>\r\n\r\n            <div style=\"padding-left: 10px;\"><em>*This row makes it easier to rehang the stitches from scrap and can be removed before binding off the shoulders if desired</em></div>\r\n            <li>Scrap off</li>\r\n        </ol>\r\n    \r\n    \r\n        <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"automatic-wrap\" data-vimeoid=\"990836499\">\r\n            <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1906648648-611a14f79d31c222ac6bc7f7a4fe333f07fa7060b292ee0a0f98aaa94ab54cdb-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n            <div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    \r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9739,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Automatic Wrap Practice",
          "slug": "automatic-wrap-practice",
          "order": 1,
